:core-eden notes

* Engine: Eden (Yuzu lineage) - GPL-3.0-or-later, consumed from /Users/ry/Desktop/claude/eden-src (local commits only; never
  push or upstream, Eden's repo forbids AI contributions).
* Bundled GPU driver: src/main/assets/eden_turnip_driver.zip = "Turnip v26.2.0-R8" (Mesa main, Vulkan 1.4.354, packaged by
  stevenmx, adrenotools format: meta.json + libvulkan_freedreno.so). It is the same file (md5 14d4ee4ddfae85673956228693f06030)
  that :core-cemu and :core-armsx2 bundle and that sits at /sdcard/_ROMs/_BIOS/Turnip_v26.2.0-R8.zip.
  Turnip is part of Mesa (freedreno), licensed under the MIT licence (Copyright Mesa contributors; Rob Clark, Google,
  Valve, Igalia et al). The MIT licence requires the copyright + permission notice to accompany copies; see
  https://docs.mesa3d.org/license.html. The driver is loaded at runtime by libadrenotools (BSD-2-Clause, bundled in Eden).
* It is enforced on every launch (EdenDriver.kt). To force the stock driver create
  /sdcard/Android/data/com.noryan.romcore/files/romcore_stock_driver.
* Vibration is permanently off (Eden's vibrator classes are stubbed in eden-src; config forced off). Asynchronous shaders are forced on every launch; create <externalFilesDir>/romcore_sync_shaders to force synchronous compilation.
